<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<handout>   
   <title>More Proofs by Contradiction</title>


    <activity workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Try to determine if the following conjectures are true on false. If true, work on the proving them by contradiction. Otherwise, find a counterexample.
        </p>

        <p>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <p>
              For each real number <m>x</m>, if <m>0&lt;x&lt;1</m> then <m>\frac{1}{x(1-x)}\ge 4</m>.
            </p>
          </li>

          <li>
            <p>
              Let <m>a, b,</m> and <m>c</m> be integers. If <m>3\mid a</m> and <m>3\mid b</m> and <m>c\equiv 1 \pmod{3}</m> then the equation <m>ax+by=c</m> has no solution in which both <m>x</m> and <m>y</m> are integers.
            </p>
          </li>

          <li>
            <p>
              For each positive real number <m>x</m>, if <m>x</m> is irrational then <m>x^2</m> is irrational.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </p>
      </statement>
    </activity>

</handout>